12","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fc70d57c562f6b93c7b525076c98e4e651a97aa0eb736e11ac3693b85c4085db","compact":"c7ca06c42ab12ed991153d457af925840646589fa6903ffa73144307770ffeea","nasal":"c7ca06c42ab12ed991153d457af925840646589fa6903ffa73144307770ffeea"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":13,"english":"Then considering it to be an unrighteous deed, with a heart moved with pity, that twice-born one, beholding the weeping Krauñci, spoke these words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3d6dc7672e214bd036dd95106c25153fc328dd2eeed616044ae0c7e89210c9b","compact":"462ec7939d64d52fe25d9b46e3cab6b96ce7113d07eb680b37003de7af09d82b","nasal":"f62a55f8b3caa1c843008f484c1da029944ba4bfd7d5d1537bad477b9383ef1f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":14,"english":"O fowler, since you have slain one of a pair of Krauñcas, you shall never attain prosperity (respect)!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a067e78ef687196d833ab620898c0f450dd1b9bfc73261943e3f161aaa93d3f2","compact":"e96e2221354d6cd7210c5f3f522c736bed62a4b6449726ec6cd7a315243a7133","nasal":"663f6c534265abaf85d1fc22d34f6aa43e66068111307e19770ab7658a451065"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":15,"english":"Having uttered this, he got worried within himself, What is this that I have said, afflicted with grief for the bird?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.908,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5ccb8ee325cd9ad344ebb94ff7e327d307dbb73360b9d77eedb08e3aaac58522","compact":"aa2c38c650a13a1b4ff6739e2d3478be28d88d7120c10853806becfd952b83be","nasal":"1ce023d3b31bf4b483538747595e0450d9e63e548bb1238fb7ace9c077befbd4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":16,"english":"Resolving thus in his mind, that highly-wise one and best of sages addressed his disciple, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.94,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5af48069e734af84ed72a9b0ee39d341623fd1f3295c0dca58de7a8ea2474ca","compact":"99b47156f59904661067fd5cbfe7426e383d6d825ff189f6c606f01719b59f05","nasal":"7f82649f0f767842980e8bd97f29d1b9a6bde305c96049cbc5164177f145ca2a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":17,"english":"This speech that I have uttered is of equal bound with metre and accents; it has rhythm and is capable of being chanted according to measure to stringed accompaniment. Let it therefore go forth as a sloka!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4467b714730d4457cc5f63d70b07c73377ddcca9978e1af782c5ba7fb2004734","compact":"1817a77fd7c335fd97a631a7de9f70b77572a3abc7add20d3a107d3e73e2f4c7","nasal":"0ff934c0a91fe9d79fde36950b523239960dab88eb5c098af7a6203c6126d797"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":18,"english":"When the sage had spoken thus, his disciple, well pleased, assented to his excellent speech; and thereat that pious person was gratified.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"df507e51844dd7cd09e3a14ee163c6b67dfa419fc4b1755b3f18fc7ca641cb6d","compact":"685be5f993f8ba19e63fdea4ce7815596ad67e800bd28ebd4e0c70fba63f8598","nasal":"5090d071bccb237194527bd4be28cb7bf465dc473948311c885cebe94595450c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":19,"english":"Then having duly performed his ablutions at that holy spot, the reverend sage retraced his steps, pondering over the incidents touching the sloka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e37cc8719bed8af4111032188d1fc852af532561dc83cca86e912c5b089993b4","compact":"03cd8f60d03f2fddef63f3280da0d856837dcca41072c985d9b5e633bd1e5ce1","nasal":"3ce1c631102bdc57c95971af6a830d007521ea9435ea43c106ab297cec0e4a5f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":20,"english":"His disciple also, accomplished in learning, and of meek demeanour, followed Vālmīki, carrying on his back a pitcher filled with water.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f4c1f3109be9ccf1972e8f03382666a9744c360ac486a888da8414a2a86af2d","compact":"2fd1f0c9748276cc8e08c075f6d09be57f1d122fa27df0622957ae04e896f273","nasal":"2fd1f0c9748276cc8e08c075f6d09be57f1d122fa27df0622957ae04e896f273"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":21,"english":"Having entered the hermitage along with his disciple, conversant with righteousness engaged in diverse kinds of talk, revolved in his mind the circumstances connected with the verses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b003a4b240ae209d42bfefb562de81b667a963af24c5a2f1a785e4ea6f8ae9a8","compact":"9419cc5e4ba30290ac781ceec02d05c77ddbe61ebea50333dc6926d427fdd1bb","nasal":"9419cc5e4ba30290ac781ceec02d05c77ddbe61ebea50333dc6926d427fdd1bb"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-22","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":22,"english":"It came to pass that desirous of seeing the best of sages, there arrived, that lord and creator of all, the effulgent Brahmā, furnished with four countenances.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.922,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002022","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"58eafb7216036ab9d2d5e5adb3d98feb62fadb138d33c4359c99dd2afa59b38c","compact":"9810d02913b4a2b793f5a08e75281567a71e28ce8856e1e68b4d08107682c47c","nasal":"9810d02913b4a2b793f5a08e75281567a71e28ce8856e1e68b4d08107682c47c"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-23","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":23,"english":"Beholding him Vālmīki rose up suddenly and, wondering greatly, humbly and silently stood before him with clasped hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.896,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002023","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0b89f0d02583c44e816dac1718958373f3a36e68d516e05fba5d60954de3367f","compact":"9b1b2bc3bdd3ef5c75ddf508a951714933ba212a802