d, O wise one, concerning Rāma, and Laksmana, and Videha's daughter, and all the Rākşasas. And even what is not known to Nārada, shall be unfolded to you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.785,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002033","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7227e69edf02f1ec5ddec5fb613ffc36cd846b93e9439dc349acdec721a974a1","compact":"a8c8f2789461e3575a90f6965739a39156e7e0d7f3f47e7859bee02ad333c889","nasal":"a8c8f2789461e3575a90f6965739a39156e7e0d7f3f47e7859bee02ad333c889"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-34","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":34,"english":"No words of yours in this poem shall contain an untruth sacred. Therefore, now compose into verses. This delightful story of Rama.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002034","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ca77ce8da413ab103bc335fa4d37806f858b3d9b33e3cfa8d2c3c0e0731602d","compact":"8aa11ece92aa7746b55fe454abf1a0ba6ed563b006bf490cee6566d4f1b89edd","nasal":"8aa11ece92aa7746b55fe454abf1a0ba6ed563b006bf490cee6566d4f1b89edd"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-2-35","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":2,"verse":35,"english":"As long as the mountains and the seas exist on earth, the history of Rāmāyaṇa will remain prevalent among men.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-2-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1002035","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"666c623e918295ae2bdcdada49110d568ba898f408c83bd2a7b47b0fef41e550","compact":"80ace7044e949a0c32a3eaf2201ce06641a79ee83b0951d1cf16d2479c1d5c74","nasal":"c95ada9e1b59da36996a7308a44f27dd1c3bbccd12bf676c07c1